@model Student
@*
    Views/Shared/_StudentRow.cshtml — SESSION PROJECT
    Session 18 — TODO 5 (Block 3), TODO 6 (Block 4), TODO 9 (Block 5)

    A PARTIAL VIEW is an ordinary .cshtml file that renders a FRAGMENT of
    a page instead of a whole page. It has no layout, no <html>, no
    <body> — just the piece. The underscore at the front of the file name
    is a convention meaning "this is not a page in its own right"; the
    same convention you have already seen on _Layout and _ViewImports.

    It lives in Views/Shared/ because Shared means "any controller's
    views may use this". Put it in Views/Students/ and only the Students
    views could find it.

    ⚠️ THIS FILE IS DELIBERATELY ALMOST EMPTY. It renders nothing until
    TODO 5 is done, which means the roster's table body will be blank the
    moment TODO 4 starts calling it and before TODO 5 fills it in. That
    order is on purpose — Block 3 wants you to see the hole before you
    fill it.
*@

